---
id: RS-004
type: rule
family: rust-reliability
title: Deserialize struct without deny_unknown_fields
version: 1

severity: info
confidence: medium
spectrum_position: 5

targets: [source]
file_extensions: [.rs]
allowlist: []

detection:
  type: ast
  ast_query: '(struct_item) @target'

related: []
enabled: true
opt_in: true
---

This struct derives `Deserialize` but is missing
`#[serde(deny_unknown_fields)]`, so it silently accepts and discards unexpected
input fields — hiding typos and protocol drift in external data. Add
`#[serde(deny_unknown_fields)]` so unknown keys become an error.

This rule is **opt-in**: it flags every named-field `Deserialize` struct, but
`deny_unknown_fields` is only warranted on structs fed by external/untrusted
input, so enable it where strict wire hygiene matters rather than by default.
Scope: named-field structs only — tuple structs, unit structs (where
`deny_unknown_fields` is a no-op) and enums are not covered.

If a struct must tolerate forward-compatible extra fields (a deliberately
lenient external contract), suppress with that reason:
`// @anvil-ignore RS-004 -- forward-compatible wire format`.
